From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ao_avfoundation: shared centre of the rebuilt output

Lucid Engine's AVFoundation audio output plays decoded PCM through
AVSampleBufferAudioRenderer, as upstream does, and passes AC-3 and E-AC-3
through AVPlayer, which upstream refuses. Its decisions are plain C that
reaches mpv, AVFoundation and the audio session only through operation
tables, so the shipped code can be driven by test fakes on the build host.

The series adds one module per patch: this shared centre, the decoded PCM
sink (0013), the passthrough start-up supervision (0014), the passthrough
sink (0015), and last the Objective-C bindings that make the Apple calls
and replace upstream's driver (0016). Each patch adds its own files to
meson.build, so every stage of the series builds; the C modules stay
unused until 0016.

This patch adds ao_avfoundation_core.h and .c: trace edges and the 8 s
detail window after each one, the prefetch guard both sinks use, the
process-wide passthrough block, the audio session steps, and the order in
which init refuses formats, sets up the session, creates the queue and
opens a sink.

Audio session: with manage-audio-session on (the default), init sets the
category and mode and activates the session, and uninit and a failed init
deactivate it, notifying other apps. With it off, the output never sets
the category or mode, activates or deactivates. Either way it declares
multichannel content for spdif formats and for more than two channels,
and sets the preferred output channel count for PCM. A PCM init clears the
passthrough block first; an spdif format with accept-compressed off is
refused before any session call.

Licence: this patch is part of Vivid's Lucid Engine patch series for mpv.
Like the mpv files it adds or changes, it is free software; you can
